--TEST--
A `class`, `interface` or `enum` declared anywhere but file scope is `E0233`, never a panic — docs/adr/README.md § *Decisions taken at project start*
--FILE--
<?nvs
// PHP declares a nested type when the statement *runs*, so whether the name
// exists depends on control flow. Novis resolves every type name against a
// static table built before any code runs — see `docs/adr/README.md`
// § *Decisions taken at project start* — so all three spellings are refused
// where they are written, by name, instead of panicking below the checker.
class Outer {
    public static function run(): int {
        class InAMethodBody {
            public int $n = 1;
        }
        return 1;
    }
}
// A block at file scope is not file scope: PHP would declare this one only
// on the branch that reaches it.
if (true) {
    interface InABlock {
        public function f(): int;
    }
}
// A closure body is a body like any other.
callable $f = fn (): int => {
    enum InAClosure: int {
        Red = 1,
    }
    return 1;
};
echo "unreached\n";

// The marker sits below the last refused line on purpose: the anchors in
// `--EXPECTF-ERROR--` are absolute, so a line added above one moves it.
// covers: lang:classes/what-a-class-cannot-declare
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0233]: a nested `class` declaration is not supported
  --> %s:9:15
  |
9 |         class InAMethodBody {
  |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `InAMethodBody` would only exist once control reached this statement
  = help: move `InAMethodBody` out to file scope — every type in Novis is declared before any code runs, so a name's existence never depends on control flow

error[E0233]: a nested `interface` declaration is not supported
   --> %s:18:15
   |
18 |     interface InABlock {
   |               ^^^^^^^^ `InABlock` would only exist once control reached this statement
   = help: move `InABlock` out to file scope — every type in Novis is declared before any code runs, so a name's existence never depends on control flow

error[E0233]: a nested `enum` declaration is not supported
   --> %s:24:10
   |
24 |     enum InAClosure: int {
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^ `InAClosure` would only exist once control reached this statement
   = help: move `InAClosure` out to file scope — every type in Novis is declared before any code runs, so a name's existence never depends on control flow

error: aborting due to 3 errors
